-- title:
--   Deformation ring surjects onto the node model 𝒪^{nr}[[U,V]]/(UV-q)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and a characteristic-zero discrete valuation ring $\mathcal{O}^{nr}$ which is a $\mathbb{Z}_q$-algebra, such that the ideal generated by the image of $q$ is maximal and $\mathcal{O}^{nr}$ is complete for that ideal, and whose residue field is algebraically closed. Let $\iota : \mathbb{Z}_{q^2} = W(\mathbb{F}_{q^2}) \to \mathcal{O}^{nr}$ be a ring homomorphism, and let $X_0$ be a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module over the residue field of $\mathcal{O}^{nr}$ relative to the reduction of $\iota$ — a two-dimensional commutative formal group law with an action of $\mathbb{Z}_{q^2}$ and an endomorphism $\varpi$ satisfying $\varpi\circ\varpi=[q]$ and $\varpi\circ[a]=[\sigma a]\circ\varpi$ — which is special (the $\iota$- and $\sigma\iota$-eigenspaces $\mathrm{Lie}_0$, $\mathrm{Lie}_1$ of the tangent space are complementary and invertible) and of height $4$ (the kernel algebra of $[q]$ is finite projective of rank $q^4$ in every fibre). Let $R$ be a Noetherian local $\mathcal{O}^{nr}$-algebra, complete for its maximal ideal, equipped with $\mathrm{res}_R : R \to k$ compatible with the residue map of $\mathcal{O}^{nr}$, together with a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module $X_u$ over $R$ and an isomorphism $w_u : X_u \otimes_{\mathrm{res}_R} k \xrightarrow{\sim} X_0$. Assume $(R,\mathrm{res}_R,X_u,w_u)$ pro-represents the deformation functor of $X_0$: for every Artinian local $\mathcal{O}^{nr}$-algebra $A$ with surjection $\mathrm{res}_A : A \to k$ compatible with the residue map, every special formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module $X$ over $A$ of height $4$ and every isomorphism $w : X\otimes_{\mathrm{res}_A} k \xrightarrow{\sim} X_0$, there is a unique $\mathcal{O}^{nr}$-algebra map $\chi : R \to A$ with $\mathrm{res}_A\circ\chi=\mathrm{res}_R$ admitting an isomorphism $v : X_u\otimes_\chi A \xrightarrow{\sim} X$ whose reduction composed with $w$ has the same power series as $w_u$. Assume finally that $X_0$ is a double point: the matrix of degree-one coefficients of the series $\varpi$ annihilates every element of $\mathrm{Lie}_0$ and of $\mathrm{Lie}_1$. Then there exists a surjective $\mathcal{O}^{nr}$-algebra homomorphism $R \to \mathcal{O}^{nr}[[U,V]]/(UV-q)$, the target being the quotient of $\mathcal{O}^{nr}$-power series in two variables by the ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - q$.
--
--   This is the existence half of Drinfeld's description of the deformation ring of a special formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module at a non-smooth (double) point, where the ring is identified with the node model $\mathcal{O}^{nr}[[U,V]]/(UV-q)$. It feeds the determination of the deformation ring in the node case and, in particular, the lower bound $2 \le \dim R$ used there.
